# Resolve Confirmation — Backend Walkthrough

## Summary

When a Purok Leader marks a concern as "resolved", it enters `awaiting_confirmation`. The citizen can confirm or dispute. **Confirmation does NOT auto-resolve** — it only flags the concern so the uw-purok frontend can unlock the resolve button. The PurokLeader must still manually resolve.

## Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant PL as Purok Leader (uw-purok)
    participant API as Backend
    participant C as Citizen (uw-citizen)

    PL->>API: PUT /concerns/{id}/status {status: "resolved"}
    API->>API: Set "awaiting_confirmation" + resolution_requested_at
    API->>C: Notification + Pusher broadcast

    alt Citizen confirms
        C->>API: POST /concerns/{id}/confirm-resolution {confirmed: true}
        API->>API: Set resolution_confirmed_at (status stays awaiting_confirmation)
        API->>PL: Notification "Resolution Confirmed"
        Note over PL: Frontend unlocks resolve button
        PL->>API: PUT /concerns/{id}/status {status: "resolved"}
        API->>API: Now sets status → "resolved"
    else Citizen disputes
        C->>API: POST /concerns/{id}/confirm-resolution {confirmed: false, reason: "..."}
        API->>API: Status → "ongoing"
        API->>PL: Notification "Resolution Disputed"
    else No response (2hr window)
        Note over PL: Frontend unlocks button after 2hrs
        PL->>API: PUT /concerns/{id}/status {status: "resolved"}
        API->>API: Sets status → "resolved"
    end
```

